If a patient has a serious-illness and has a poor-functional-prognosis then an opioid may be an appropriate-therapy during a previous-therapy-history.
If a patient has an alternative-therapy-contraindication then an opioid may be an appropriate-therapy during a previous-therapy-history.
If a clinician has a patient-comfort-agreement then an opioid may be an appropriate-therapy during a previous-therapy-history.
